Seems most everyone hates per-role scaling.  I expected disagreement
about the specific numbers, not so much about the basic idea.

So--  what I'll do is axe the entire per-role factor and replace with
role-specific feats that give more opportunities for 'bonus' score to
roles that are harder to start.

Feats will still be conditional to avoid changing savegame formats
without enabling them.  Those in the below list with a (*) will
probably be implementable without savegame changes.

Here are my current ideas:  (I'm working on the patch; will post soon)

"big" bonuses:
- Tourists get points for every species (*) and 'historical' statue
photographed
- Archaeologists get a (bigger) bonus for every level explored (*)
- Healers I haven't figured out yet

The "medium" bonus roles would get an early-game survival bonus, say,
that stretches to (and caps at) turn 20000 for every turn survived.
(*)

Easy roles don't get specific feats.

How's that?

